impl.risks_left:
- **Nothing has been compiled or run.** Parse-checking only catches reader errors. Wrong arity, names or kondo warnings would only show at build or test time.
- **Johan's override is unverified.** It lives in ~/OneDrive, which I did not read. If its NEXT (or NOW) differs from the reconstructed 0.10.x template in any way (another join, an extra clause, a different marker set type), that query stays on the slow d/q path unchanged. The q-fastpath log lines will show which queries hit.
- **Exactness relies on:**
  - datascript's built-in `<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=` agreeing with cljs comparison on numbers (they use value-compare; non-numbers fall back);
  - scalar page constants comparing the same way in d/q and in `d/datoms`, which holds for non-ref, non-tuple attributes and scalar constants.
- **Row order changes.** d/q returned rows in hash-set order; the fast path returns them by page journal day, then entity id. NOW re-sorts by priority, and NEXT now has a stable order.
- **Out of scope, as the critique listed:**
  - the scheduled/deadlines query on the journals home (about 410 ms at 10k);
  - linked references;
  - evicting previous-day today-query keys;
  - the `:block/journal?` compat rewrite.
